.TH SDL_RenderDebugTextFormat 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_RenderDebugTextFormat \- Draw debug text to an
.BR SDL_Renderer .

.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_render.h>
.PP
.BI "bool SDL_RenderDebugTextFormat(SDL_Renderer *renderer, float x, float y, const char *fmt, ...);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This function will render a printf()-style format string to a renderer\[char46] Note that this is a convenience function for debugging, with severe limitations, and is not intended to be used for production apps and games\[char46]
.PP
For the full list of limitations and other useful information, see
.BR SDL_RenderDebugText \[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I renderer
the renderer which should draw the text\[char46]
.TP
.I x
the x coordinate where the top-left corner of the text will draw\[char46]
.TP
.I y
the y coordinate where the top-left corner of the text will draw\[char46]
.TP
.I fmt
the format string to draw\[char46]
.TP
.I ...
additional parameters matching % tokens in the
.BR fmt
string, if any\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns true on success or false on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
This function should only be called on the main thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_RenderDebugText (3),
.BR SDL_DEBUG_TEXT_FONT_CHARACTER_SIZE (3)
